@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "About this build";
    ViewData["Description"] = "How Harry Potter Explorer is put together.";
}

<div class="shell stack" style="max-width:900px">
    <header class="page-head">
        <p class="eyebrow">Colophon</p>
        <h1>About this build</h1>
        <p>
            Harry Potter Explorer is an ASP.NET Core MVC application. It has no client framework,
            no build step and no external service calls from the browser.
        </p>
    </header>

    <section class="panel">
        <h2>Where the data comes from</h2>
        <p>
            Characters and spells are read from the public
            <a href="https://hp-api.onrender.com/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">hp-api.onrender.com</a>
            by a background service on the server, then written into a local SQLite database. Pages
            and the JSON API read that database, never the upstream host. That is why the site keeps
            working when the upstream instance is asleep, and why searching feels instant.
        </p>
        <p>
            House lore and the artefact vault have no upstream source. They are curated content kept
            in the repository — a C# catalogue for the houses, a JSON file for the artefacts — and
            loaded into the same database on start.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="panel">
        <h2>Your collection</h2>
        <p>
            The cards you keep live in your browser&rsquo;s <code>localStorage</code>. The server is told
            only that a card was collected or released, tagged with an anonymous per-browser id so one
            visitor cannot inflate the public tally. There is no account, no email and nothing to log in to.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="panel">
        <h2>The public API</h2>
        <p>Everything the pages use is available as JSON:</p>
        <ul class="small">
            <li><a href="/api/characters?pageSize=5"><code>GET /api/characters</code></a> — search, filter, page</li>
            <li><code>GET /api/characters/{id}</code> — one character in full</li>
            <li><a href="/api/spells?pageSize=5"><code>GET /api/spells</code></a> — the spellbook</li>
            <li><a href="/api/artifacts"><code>GET /api/artifacts</code></a> — the vault</li>
            <li><a href="/api/houses"><code>GET /api/houses</code></a> — house lore with member counts</li>
            <li><a href="/api/stats"><code>GET /api/stats</code></a> — live aggregates and mirror status</li>
            <li><code>POST /api/sync</code> — ask for an out-of-band refresh</li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="panel">
        <h2>Credits</h2>
        <p class="small muted">
            A fan-made, non-commercial study project. The wizarding world, its names and its
            characters belong to their respective rights holders. Character images are served from
            the upstream API&rsquo;s own image host.
        </p>
    </section>
</div>
